# i18n Translations

When working on UI changes (adding screens, copy edits, new buttons, error messages, accessibility labels, etc.), **only add, remove, or update keys in `locales/en/*.json`**. Do not edit, add, or remove translations in any other language catalog (`locales/{es,fr,de,it,ja,zh-Hans,ar}/*.json`). Translations are reviewed and committed independently, often by the user.

## What to do

- Add new keys under the appropriate namespace in `locales/en/`:
  - `common.json` — shared actions ("Cancel", "OK", "Done")
  - `tabs.json`, `home.json`, `row.json`, `settings.json`, `sensor.json`, `ble.json`, `modal.json` — screen-specific
- Reference keys in components via `useTranslation("<namespace>")` and `t("path.to.key")`.
- Use ICU MessageFormat for plurals/selects/numbers, e.g. `"{count, number}"`, `"{direction, select, rtl {…} other {…}}"`.

## What NOT to do

- Do not edit files under `locales/es/`, `locales/fr/`, `locales/de/`, `locales/it/`, `locales/ja/`, `locales/zh-Hans/`, or `locales/ar/`.
- Do not invent translations or "best-effort" stubs in the non-English catalogs.
- Do not block on missing translations: i18next falls back to `en` automatically when a key is missing in the active language, so the UI never breaks.

## Adding a new language

If asked to add a brand-new language, that's an exception to this rule — see `lib/i18n/resources.ts` and `lib/i18n/languages.ts` for the registration pattern.
